<section image-layout="blank" id="5s82U58uaU" background-color="palette-4"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="XgYs3KvHvV" background-color="palette-4" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">TEACH IT BACK</p><h1 font-size="36pt">Your 20-second shield story</h1><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size:30pt; --marker-gap:12pt;"><grid-item id="McqTWVnuN3" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Where?</b> In the stratosphere, above the weather.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IjTi_vPBtC" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Its job?</b> Absorb much harmful UV; some still passes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Nv2ptvmcJG" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>What thinned it?</b> Long-lived human-made chemicals.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="m2TxOvpbiX" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>What helps?</b> Countries phasing those chemicals out together.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item background-color="palette-3" padding="12pt 16pt"><h4>Finish strong</h4><p font-size="18pt">Name one real action, then correct one mix-up: sun safety protects people now; it does not repair ozone.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="5xBM1D6WpK" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/U-xDlB-5f2pctyAXHy_52.png" saved-media-id="eg2qgh3t3r7vfnx" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="atmosphere-cut-paper" alt="Layered cut-paper editorial science illustration of a curious ten-year-old pointing toward an Earth cutaway at the lower right, the Earth in the same orientation as a curved cloud-white surface beneath a thin shield-blue atmospheric arc, UV-gold rays arriving from the upper left with some stopping in the arc and one continuing, a small action-green circle suggesting cooperation, deep-ink space, clean vector-like edges, subtle paper fibers, confident optimistic classroom tone, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>